<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Apple's privacy manifest, required for App Store submission.

  Updated 2026-11-21 (James: the phone app recognises the suite sign-in).
  It was "Data Not Collected" from 2026-10-12. What it collects now, and only
  when the phone already holds a UNI·SIM session that ANOTHER suite app made
  (the shared Keychain group co.uk.unisim.suite):

  - No sign-in of its own. The phone build sets @unisim/sdk's `noAccounts`
    and `signInInTune: false` (src/main.tsx, src/lib/accounts.ts): no Sign in,
    no account screens, no "the app was opened" event (<UsageTracker /> stays
    off). It reads the session the device holds and follows it.
  - Name and Email Address, linked, App Functionality + Product
    Personalization: the desk's title becomes "Bradley's PDFs"
    (src/native/personalTitle.ts, the SDK's useCallMe: Global Tuning's Call
    me, else the profile's name, else a name-shaped email).
  - User ID, linked, App Functionality: the account id the session carries,
    which keys the reads and writes below.
  - Other Data Types, linked, App Functionality: Tune this app's choices
    (colour scheme, language, default views) are saved to the account's
    `tune:pdf` row and read back (the SDK's TuneSync), with the account's
    Global Tuning and its choice of the app's title.

  Nothing else changes:

  - No uploads. Signing and "Send for signature" happen on the phone: each
    "Sign here" box becomes a real PDF signature field and the file leaves
    through the system share sheet, to wherever the user sends it, never to
    us. The certified-signature route (stored copy, emailed link, certificate)
    is the website's only and is not in the phone app at all.
  - No usage count. The SDK's anonymous daily open count is off in the shell
    (`openCount: !isDesktop && !isNativeShell()`), and the suite user count it
    replaced (an install id) was retired in @unisim/sdk 0.187.0.
  - Signing on another phone (the QR handoff) relays the drawing as an
    ephemeral Realtime broadcast with a PIN: nothing is stored and nothing
    identifies the user, so it is not "collected" in Apple's sense.
  - The iOS Scan button is Apple's VisionKit (DocumentScanner.swift), which
    sends nothing. (The Android scanner's ML Kit diagnostics are declared in
    Play's Data safety answers, store-assets/data-safety.json; they do not
    apply here.)

  Nothing is used for tracking, and there are no third-party analytics or
  advertising SDKs.

  Required-reason APIs: @capacitor/filesystem reads file creation and
  modification dates (its `stat`), only on files in the app's own container,
  and it ships no manifest of its own. Capacitor's core frameworks carry their
  own manifests for what they use, so they are not repeated here.

  Keep this in step with the App Store Connect privacy answers (Name, Email
  Address, User ID, Other Data Types: linked, not tracking; see
  Docs_UNI_SIM/store-listings/universal-pdf.md) and PRIVACY.md.
-->
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<!-- @capacitor/filesystem's stat: files in the app container. C617.1. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<!-- The name in the desk's title, from a suite session the phone holds. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeName</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeProductPersonalization</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<!-- The session's email: the name falls back to it. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeEmailAddress</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeProductPersonalization</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<!-- The account id the session carries. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeUserID</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<!-- Tune this app settings kept with the account (TuneSync). -->
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeOtherDataTypes</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
